Fillets: past the end of a spine, where a contact leaves its face and no
face follows, the blend rolls on the face's own surface (unbounded) when
that surface is a cylinder, cone, sphere or torus (mitcad#121, with 0075).

ChFi3d_BuildPlane continued the walk on the plane tangent to the face at
the point where the previous piece's contact crossed the face's edge ("till
the output on the other face"). The previous piece rolled on the surface
itself, often past that edge already (with the overflow patches), so the
two pieces solved for different balls where they meet: a gap between their
sections (0.03 in a rounding round a chamfered bar with radius 3, which
made the face builder drop part of a planar face with the rolling ball of
0075; 0.015 before it). On an elementary surface the face's own surface,
made into a face without edges, continues exactly; other surfaces keep the
tangent plane (their natural bounds could stop the walk).
